Package: mooncam
Version: @VERSION@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: dotnet-runtime-10.0, libavcodec62 | libavcodec61 | libavcodec60,
 linux-modules-v4l2loopback-generic-hwe-26.04 | linux-modules-v4l2loopback-generic | linux-modules-v4l2loopback-oem-26.04,
 adb, avahi-utils, network-manager, pkexec, kmod
Conflicts: v4l2loopback-dkms (>= 0~)
Maintainer: Moon Technologies <https://github.com/Moon-TechnologiesCO>
Homepage: https://github.com/Moon-TechnologiesCO/MoonCam
Description: Use your Android phone as a webcam for Linux
 MoonCam turns an Android phone into a webcam for this computer, over USB or
 Wi-Fi. The video appears as a real camera ("MoonCam") in OBS Studio, Discord,
 Zoom, Google Meet and browsers. Local only: no cloud, no account, no telemetry.
